            <ArticleTitle>A hip resurfacing implant in an adolescent with cerebral palsy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>167-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/BPB.0b013e328344e809</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain or skin irritation due to the femoral stump after proximal femoral resection for chronic spastic hip dislocation in children with severe cerebral palsy may be encountered. We describe a technique that, to our knowledge, has been unreported earlier and can deal with this phenomenon to improve the patient's comfort level and help the patient to sit more comfortably.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
